DISCHARGED ASSUMPTIONS, as a premise role (@ajs's choice):
- a PREMISE_OF link can be marked `assumed`;
- the step that discharges it (a contradiction or an induction step) says so;
- the conclusion then no longer depends on that assumption;
- the read-back shows "assumed, discharged by …".

ARBITRARY VARIABLES, declared and checked (@ajs's choice):
- a step declares the variables it generalizes over;
- reflow2 checks that no premise in the chain fixes them, i.e. names a specific value for them.
This is a structural check, not a full logic.

From the primes trial, item 5 (F6, F7), and fact:the-methods-of-proof-mostly-fit-an-inference-and-three-need-more-2026-10-14. @ajs, 2026-10-17.
